    "license": "CC0",
    "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en",
    "description": "The fish in the image is scientifically known as Sillago sihama and is most commonly called the Lady Fish or Silver Whiting. In the coastal regions of Karnataka, it is known as Kane in both Kannada and Tulu. Characterized by its slender, cylindrical body and a distinctly pointed snout, this seawater fish features a silvery-white underside that transitions into a pale brown or golden hue along its back. It possesses two dorsal fins and a slightly forked tail, which together allow it to be an agile swimmer in sandy coastal waters. Its scales are small and smooth to the touch, and its flesh is highly prized for being lean, white, and exceptionally tender with a delicate flavor. Because it contains only a single central bone, it is a favorite for traditional preparations like the Mangalorean Kane Rava Fry, where its soft texture is complemented by a crispy semolina coating.",
